Declaration lists the author wrapped after a trailing comma (:DECLARE,
:PARAMETERS, :PUBLIC): the trailing comma keeps the statement open and
the continuation keeps its indent across passes (fmt.max_line_length
issue #218 note on wrapped :DECLARE lists; fmt.indent_style). Records
where continuation items land.
-- input.ssl --
:PARAMETERS sSampleId, sTestCode,
sAnalyst, dRunDate;
:DEFAULT sAnalyst, "";
:PUBLIC gnSessionCount,
gsSessionUser;
:DECLARE sStatus, nAttempt,
         bDone,
  aRows;
sStatus := "";
-- format --
:PARAMETERS sSampleId, sTestCode,
            sAnalyst, dRunDate;
:DEFAULT sAnalyst, "";
:PUBLIC gnSessionCount,
        gsSessionUser;
:DECLARE sStatus, nAttempt,
         bDone,
         aRows;

sStatus := "";
